+# Persistent placement checkpoint
+
+Studio 5.329.97 / SDK 0.10 delivers persistent visual motherboard-part placement in Chapter creator: project-owned immutable mesh/license/provenance packs, native Preview/Apply, typed transforms, Undo/Redo, Save and restart. Separate frozen create/reopen processes preserved every field and saved byte; actual native viewport/picking/isolated Play passed. Debug and Release each passed 59 tests; both installed SDK consumers passed; 183 Python/Qt and 68 packaging tests passed. All five existing launchers were backed up and now open97. S5BP is complete; S5B textures/lighting and the wider M5 alpha remain in progress. Studio96/95, SDK0.9/0.8, public87, original memoir/photos, real saves and separate Unreal remain preserved.
+
+Open an existing Studio shortcut → Engineering Labs → AI-BS Game Engine Build → Chapter creator. Open/create a chapter, Use bundled sample part → Preview asset placement → Apply preview → Save chapter. Keep the whole project folder, including assets/packs.
+
+The cumulative source/evidence archive excludes compiled distributions, model weights, memoir/photo originals, real saves and the separate Unreal project. Synthetic acceptance projects are explicitly labelled proof workspaces. Local archive CRC/per-file SHA and independent review accompany Drive metadata readback; remote byte hashes/account quota are unavailable.
+
+Next: Extend UV/tangent and image import with actual native texture sampling, then material/lighting paths while preserving chapter placement/save compatibility; continue M5 personal pacing/audio/settings.
+
+Drive: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12tZrIZmt1mQtyd3Tt_OeAAE-gJoWTG5k
